  (3) THE CORRECTNESS GATE IS MEASURED ON SERVED OUTPUT (lesson L2).
  kickoff_contract_approved asks that the kickoff contract state the correctness gate
  as a served-output comparison against the reference - task accuracy for a model
  port, the feature's observable output for a feature port - with its pass rule, and
  register every intermediate-tensor tolerance as a diagnostic that selects no
  outcome; the question names its defect - a tensor gate measures the stack, not the
  port. Before: the check accepted "thresholds, methods" at any level;
  assemble_kickoff_contracts now points at the check's served-output form, so a
  contract is not drafted flat and refused at gate 1. Evidence: the kickoff contract
